# One line ending everywhere, so a build is a function of the source and not
# of the machine that ran it.
#
# Git checks out CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux. The zip is built from the
# working tree, so the same commit produced two different zips: 66 of 123
# members of 0.0.4 differed, every one of them by newlines alone. Fixing the
# timestamps made the build reproducible on one machine; this makes it
# reproducible across them, which is what "the release and the published zip
# are the same" actually requires - otherwise it can only ever be checked
# against the machine that happened to publish.
#
# LF rather than CRLF because that is what is already stored, what the
# Android boxes run, and what Kodi's own add-ons use.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Left exactly as they are. `text=auto` detects most of these on its own, but
# a frozen test fixture that git decided to "fix" would be a very confusing
# afternoon.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.zip    binary
*.db     binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
